    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "36236844_3faeaac3",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/render/MeshRenderStep.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 32
      },
      "lineNbr": 183,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-09T14:35:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Gotcha, I didn\u0027t realize that the SkRuntimeEffect::Uniform\u0027s name was a string_view instead of a std::string.  We could always update Graphite\u0027s Uniform to have a string_view instead of a const char* but that doesn\u0027t buy us much since the name is only used here for debugging.\n\nHow about this plan:\n\n1. Bring back the name copying and building the full uniform array, but guard all of that by an `#if defined(SK_DEBUG)`, since the uniform array and names are only going to be used by the UniformExpectationsValidator.\n\n2. Inside the main for loop calling write(), we can just use a single stack allocated Uniform inside the loop that has a null name with a comment outlining that we only need the type information. That way in release builds we aren\u0027t allocating anything while writing uniforms.",
      "parentUuid": "99ad6c9c_1c06d74e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 183,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 183,
        "endChar": 52
      },
      "revId": "1461d8bd91e610425d8d6a6a50d4c797ddc21741",
